<title>POLAND: Polish crop ratings improve in June 20-30.</title>
<headline>Polish crop ratings improve in June 20-30.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Meteorology and Water Management Institute (IMGW) said crop evaluations in the third 10 days of June were slightly better than the previous 10-day period and stayed above 1996 and five-year average levels.</p>
<p>Ratings are made three times a month based on the condition and development of crops on a scale of one to five, with five the highest grade.</p>
<p>POLISH CROP RATINGS   JUNE 30   JUNE 20  1996  5-YR AVG</p>
<p>Wheat (winter)	  3.6	 3.6     3.6	3.5</p>
<p>Wheat (summer)	  3.7	 3.6     3.6	3.4</p>
<p>Rye			 3.7	 3.6     3.6	3.5</p>
<p>Barley (spring)	 3.8	 3.7     3.6	3.3</p>
<p>Rapeseed (winter)     3.1	 3.0     2.8	3.2</p>
<p>Oats			3.7	 3.6     3.6	3.4</p>
<p>Sugar beets	     3.7	 3.5     3.6	3.4</p>
<p>Potatoes		  3.7	 3.6     3.6	3.4</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
